    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Tucked away in the extremely private and intimate setting of Kilcolman Court, this beautifully presented three-bedroom home offers an appealing combination of excellent natural light, privacy, mature gardens and genuine extension potential.\r\nWith approximately 20 homes in the development, Kilcolman Court has a peaceful, established feel while remaining exceptionally well located for transport links, local amenities and the coast, including the iconic Forty Foot and Killiney Hill.\r\nExtending to approximately 1,000 sq. ft., the house has recently been redecorated and is presented in lovely condition throughout. Accommodation comprises three bedrooms, one bathroom, Living\\dining room and a kitchen/breakfast room.\r\nThe property enjoys a wonderful open outlook to the front, with a south-westerly aspect providing excellent natural light and afternoon and evening sunshine.\r\nThe outdoor space is a real highlight and boasts beautifully maintained gardens. The front patio enjoys the open aspect, facing directly onto the green and enjoying a sunny south-westerly orientation, while the rear garden has been lovingly maintained and planted with established shrubs and trees. A further patio provides an ideal space for outdoor dining and relaxation and incorporates a genuine Chiminea and large pots of plants. At the end of the garden is a large garden shed/outdoor room, offering versatile additional space. Beyond this is a further rear area, with each property in the development having its own designated space for a shed.\r\nThe nearby coastline and Forty Foot, Dun Laoghaire Piers and Yacht clubs, offer superb opportunities for swimming, walking and enjoying the outdoors, while cafés, restaurants, shops and everyday amenities are readily accessible as is Dalkey Heritage Town. In all, there are three entrances into the development. A vehicular one from Upper Glenageary Road and two pedestrian entrances, one onto Adelaide Road and one onto Marlborough Road with Glenageary Dart station located at the bottom. There are also a wide selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools close at hand."
      },
